=== X1. cdc_acm: what the kernel config says when the driver folder is missing
-- FAKE_ACM=m
cdc_acm   : NOT LOADED - this kernel has the driver as a module. Try:  su -c 'modprobe cdc_acm'  and run spft check again
-- FAKE_ACM=y
cdc_acm   : not found, although the kernel config says it is built in. If the target is never detected, use another host phone (or mtkclient)
-- FAKE_ACM=n
cdc_acm   : MISSING - this kernel was built without it (CONFIG_USB_ACM), so SP Flash Tool can't see a device from this phone (use mtkclient instead)
-- FAKE_ACM=none
cdc_acm   : not found, and the kernel config can't be read to tell why. If the target is never detected, use another host phone (or mtkclient)
-- FAKE_ACM=(option not in the config)
cdc_acm   : MISSING - this kernel was built without it (CONFIG_USB_ACM), so SP Flash Tool can't see a device from this phone (use mtkclient instead)

